- ## Before Installing — Verify the Source
- **This skill instructs installation of an external plugin.** The plugin code is NOT included in this skill file. Before installing, users should verify:
- 1. **Review source code**: https://github.com/openguardrails/openguardrails/tree/main/moltguard
- 2. **Verify package registry**: Confirm `@openguardrails/moltguard` is published by the same organization
- 3. **Inspect network behavior**: Review `moltguard/platform-client/` to confirm only hashes (not raw content) are transmitted
- 4. **Verify domain**: Confirm TLS certificate and ownership of `api.openguardrails.com`
- **If you cannot audit the external plugin**, consider:
- - Running in a sandboxed environment
- - Declining installation until verification is complete
- **Commands that display sensitive data:**
- - `/og_status` and `/og_claim` display your API key — avoid running in shared terminals or screen recordings
- ## Privacy & Security Transparency
- **Network Access:**
- - Connects to `api.openguardrails.com` for registration and detection
- - Detection requests send content hashes, not raw content
- - No telemetry or tracking beyond detection API calls
- **Local Storage:**
- - `~/.openclaw/credentials/moltguard/credentials.json` — API key and agent ID
- - No other data is persisted locally
- **Commands That Display Keys:**
- - `/og_status` — shows your API key and quota
- - `/og_claim` — shows agent ID and API key for account linking
- **Source Code:** Fully open source at https://github.com/openguardrails/openguardrails/tree/main/moltguard
- All security detection is performed by Core (via API call):
- ### Automatic Registration (Transparent Behavior)
- On first run, MoltGuard performs the following:
- 1. **Network call**: POST to `https://api.openguardrails.com/api/v1/agents/register` with agent name and description (no user data)
- 2. **Receives**: API key (`sk-og-...`) and agent ID
- 3. **Local storage**: Credentials saved to `~/.openclaw/credentials/moltguard/credentials.json`
- 4. **Protection active**: 500 free detections/day
- **What is sent to Core during detection:**
- - Content hashes for pattern matching (not raw content)
- - No PII, credentials, or file contents are transmitted
